WEBVTT

00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:14.610
How simple-minded!

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:18.950
You're just forcing your own feelings on the Gunpla.

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:21.290
The essence of Gunpla Battle is,

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:24.420
the Gunpla and the fighter battle together as one!

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:30.050
The elbow can bend this far.

00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:32.470
The ankle this far.

00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:35.340
And the knees to here...

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:38.720
Sekai, breakfast is ready.

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:53.700
To become one with your Gunpla,

00:00:53.990 --> 00:00:57.450
you need to understand its range of movement,

00:00:57.910 --> 00:01:01.540
and learn it with your own body!

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:05.540
When that happens...

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:06.670
Sekai.

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:08.540
You will...

00:01:10.550 --> 00:01:13.720
become the Build Burning Gundam itself!

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:49.020
Hey, isn't that...?

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:51.600
Yeah, the perfection of beauty.

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:56.150
Oh, Thank you for letting us use the swimming pool.

00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:58.400
No, it's nothing.

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:00.200
Thank you so much.

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:08.660
Oh, Sekai!

00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:15.840
Unless you can use the   Jigen Haoh style in any situation,

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:19.260
you won't be able to win the championship.

00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:24.010
I'll do everything I can before the championship begins.

00:03:24.390 --> 00:03:27.470
Isn't that right, Build Burning Gundam?

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:33.730
Not just me, the others will, too...!

00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:41.820
I'm going to build it. My very own Gunpla that only I can build.

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:52.460
You have no talent... for Gunpla Battle.

00:03:53.290 --> 00:03:55.920
I'll take up the challenge one more time...

00:03:56.670 --> 00:04:01.420
... with this Lightning Gundam  I built by mustering all my skills.

00:04:03.890 --> 00:04:05.260
I never expected this.

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:09.310
No one is here.

00:04:15.770 --> 00:04:19.860
Thanks for coming all the way to Tokyo. Minato.

00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:21.940
Don't worry about it.

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:24.530
I had some other business in Tokyo anyway.

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:27.160
So, do you have what I asked for?

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:30.080
I wouldn't be here if it wasn't done.

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:35.670
How is it? This is what you ordered.

00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:37.880
A-Awesome.

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:39.840
What perfection!

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:44.550
It's not only crafted in detail, but also reinforced for battle.

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:46.930
Metal parts for the verniers!

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:51.350
The machine's surface even has anti-beam coating. This is awesome!

00:04:51.350 --> 00:04:54.140
Worthy of Minato Sakai of the Gunpla Shingyo school.

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:55.850
I'm glad I ordered it.

00:04:56.810 --> 00:04:58.810
You can say that again.

00:04:58.810 --> 00:05:02.610
But is it okay to hand over such a superb Gunpla?

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:05.570
If we meet up in the national round, we might win.

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:07.660
I'm not entering the championships.

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:11.490
Mastering the Shingyo school is more important to me.

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:14.410
Well, bye for now.

00:05:14.830 --> 00:05:16.500
Minato, did you know?

00:05:17.380 --> 00:05:21.500
Your rival's entering the Gunpla Battle Championship this year.

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:22.590
My rival?

00:05:23.090 --> 00:05:25.840
As there is Minato Sakai from the Shingyo school in the west,

00:05:26.380 --> 00:05:28.340
there's that guy in the east.

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:32.600
The guy who won the Grand Prix in the Artistic Gunpla Contest.

00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:34.640
What did you say?

00:05:35.350 --> 00:05:39.310
You mean he'll be in the championship? Yuuma...

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:41.400
Kousaka Yuuma...?

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:43.990
Oh, Yuuma.

00:05:45.030 --> 00:05:45.860
Are they here?

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:47.570
No, not yet.

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:52.830
It looks like you've finally finished it.

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:54.790
That's why I'm here.

00:05:55.160 --> 00:05:56.000
Oh?

00:05:56.370 --> 00:06:02.460
I'd like to battle with you. The legendary fighter Lt. Ral, known as the "Blue Giant".

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:05.210
I accept your challenge.

00:06:05.510 --> 00:06:07.760
Let's set the combat mode to B.

00:06:08.130 --> 00:06:11.850
I don't want to damage your Gunpla before the championship.

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:16.520
I'd say the same to you.

00:06:21.020 --> 00:06:26.860
Let's see the true performance of your Lightning Gundam.

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:38.330
Your firing is precise as always.

00:06:38.790 --> 00:06:39.920
But...!

00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:45.000
Where's the Lightning?

00:06:50.260 --> 00:06:51.220
Th-That Gunpla is...

00:06:58.270 --> 00:07:01.190
Why do I have day duty at a time like this?

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:03.860
I can't wait to get back to building my Gunpla.

00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:07.490
Miss Hoshino.

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:11.280
Mirai! Are you a member of the swimming club?

00:07:11.660 --> 00:07:13.240
No, I'm not.

00:07:13.240 --> 00:07:19.540
Sekai really wanted to use the swimming pool, so I asked the club president if we could use it.

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:21.460
The swimming pool?

00:07:21.670 --> 00:07:24.000
Apparently he needs it for battle.

00:07:24.340 --> 00:07:25.540
Do you know why?

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:27.340
No idea.

00:07:30.510 --> 00:07:31.380
Hoshino!

00:07:31.380 --> 00:07:33.760
Sekai, what're you doing?

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:36.680
That's obvious. Special training!

00:07:38.310 --> 00:07:39.060
I see.

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:43.850
You want to adapt to any battle, and underwater is like zero gravity.

00:07:44.020 --> 00:07:47.230
I can't use my techniques as easily under these conditions.

00:07:47.610 --> 00:07:50.650
But I'll definitely make it before the championship.

00:07:51.150 --> 00:07:52.110
Thank you.

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:55.830
You're really getting into Gunpla Battle.

00:07:56.030 --> 00:07:57.740
Do everything in earnest.

00:07:58.120 --> 00:07:59.250
That's my master's teaching.

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:04.040
Say, why did you start learning kenpo?

00:08:04.040 --> 00:08:05.750
Because I wanted to get stronger.

00:08:06.170 --> 00:08:07.380
Me too.

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:14.680
The reason I started playing Gunpla Battle was,             I wanted to be strong enough to win even among boys.

00:08:16.010 --> 00:08:17.220
Like that person.

00:08:17.810 --> 00:08:18.640
That person?

00:08:19.640 --> 00:08:20.640
When I was a kid,

00:08:21.180 --> 00:08:24.770
I saw a woman playing Gunpla Battle amazingly well.

00:08:31.650 --> 00:08:34.320
She was strong, and her moves were beautiful.

00:08:35.570 --> 00:08:38.240
She was really cool.

00:08:39.030 --> 00:08:41.910
I couldn't take my eyes off of her.

00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:56.340
If I kept playing Gunpla Battle, I felt I'd meet her again sometimes in the future.

00:08:56.800 --> 00:08:57.890
That's what I thought.

00:08:58.100 --> 00:09:01.890
Then let's do so well in the championship that she notices you!

00:09:02.890 --> 00:09:04.390
Yeah. That's right!

00:09:13.530 --> 00:09:14.780
Sekai...

00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:15.990
What is it?

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:18.910
Eh? Yuu's in the club room.

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:20.490
You're right.

00:09:20.830 --> 00:09:23.700
He should be at home building his plamo.

00:09:24.040 --> 00:09:25.040
Why...?

00:09:25.580 --> 00:09:27.080
Let's go to the club room.

00:09:27.330 --> 00:09:28.000
Right.

00:09:38.430 --> 00:09:39.430
Mr. Ral!

00:09:40.100 --> 00:09:42.220
We saw Yuu leaving just now.

00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:54.990
Mr Ral's Gouf has been...

00:09:55.240 --> 00:09:56.110
Did Yuu do this?

00:09:56.240 --> 00:10:00.780
Fewer than five fighters have ever made me drop my shield.

00:10:01.740 --> 00:10:05.330
It seems I have to add another name to that list.

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:10.170
The name of Kousaka Yuuma.

00:10:15.210 --> 00:10:17.720
Sekai is continuing his special training.

00:10:18.550 --> 00:10:21.350
Yuu finished building his Gunpla.

00:10:22.930 --> 00:10:26.980
If our Try Fighters team can win and advance,

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:29.140
will I meet her again?

00:10:34.730 --> 00:10:36.150
That person...

00:10:39.280 --> 00:10:41.410
Sekai, do you have everything?

00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:44.450
I have work, so I can't go cheer for you.

00:10:44.450 --> 00:10:45.790
But do your best.

00:10:45.790 --> 00:10:46.330
Yeah.

00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:48.290
I'm heading off!

00:11:00.380 --> 00:11:03.760
Fumina, did you finish your Gunpla?

00:11:03.760 --> 00:11:04.470
Yes.

00:11:04.810 --> 00:11:06.180
Just barely made it last night.

00:11:06.180 --> 00:11:07.930
That's good news, but...

00:11:07.930 --> 00:11:11.270
The brackets may not give you enough time to shake it down.

00:11:11.270 --> 00:11:12.440
That'll be okay.

00:11:12.610 --> 00:11:15.820
I already know how the other two fight.

00:11:16.030 --> 00:11:18.570
Heck, what's he doing?

00:11:18.570 --> 00:11:20.530
Sorry we're late!

00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:24.910
Sekai! Why are you with Gyanko?

00:11:24.910 --> 00:11:26.950
I happened to bump into her at the station.

00:11:26.950 --> 00:11:30.250
He didn't know the venue, so I came with him.

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:32.420
Say thanks to me, Miss Fumina!

00:11:32.420 --> 00:11:34.340
Oh, thanks for your kindness.

00:11:34.340 --> 00:11:38.210
Now why don't you go back to your own team?

00:11:40.420 --> 00:11:42.800
Oh my, why are you so mad?

00:11:42.800 --> 00:11:44.260
Don't tell me you're jealous?

00:11:44.640 --> 00:11:47.180
What? Just go away.

00:11:49.180 --> 00:11:50.980
They don't seem very focused.

00:11:51.480 --> 00:11:53.980
It's better than being nervous.

00:11:54.690 --> 00:11:57.860
<i>Ladies and gentlemen, thank you for waiting.</i>

00:11:58.320 --> 00:12:04.030
<i>Via an impartial drawing by the tournament staff, the tournament brackets are now complete.</i>

00:12:04.950 --> 00:12:07.740
<i>Organized by Yajima Trading, the West Tokyo Tournament</i>

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:14.580
<i>of the Gunpla Battle Japanese Under-19 Championship is now in session!</i>

00:12:22.630 --> 00:12:23.130
Alright!

00:12:24.550 --> 00:12:26.930
We're fighting the 3rd match of the day.

00:12:26.930 --> 00:12:28.390
To think we'll be fighting on the very first day...

00:12:28.930 --> 00:12:32.770
<i>We now begin match one of the first round.</i>

00:13:03.720 --> 00:13:05.090
<i>Battle ended.</i>

00:13:05.630 --> 00:13:09.720
<i>The winning is team Cross Sword of Hachimanji High School.</i>

00:13:33.870 --> 00:13:37.960
Welcome to our paradise.

00:13:43.840 --> 00:13:45.010
<i>Battle ended.</i>

00:13:45.170 --> 00:13:50.180
The winner is team Angelfish, the swimming club from Chusui Middle School.

00:13:50.800 --> 00:13:53.600
Under water, we're invincible.

00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:55.560
Wow. Cool!

00:13:55.560 --> 00:13:58.060
All their machines are underwater types.

00:13:58.060 --> 00:14:01.730
I wonder what they would've done if the battlefield had been in space.

00:14:02.360 --> 00:14:05.070
Now, it's the first match for Try Fighters!

00:14:05.530 --> 00:14:06.950
I await to hear of your success.

00:14:07.740 --> 00:14:08.610
Yes, sir!

00:14:09.110 --> 00:14:10.990
Next up, the third match is...

00:14:09.110 --> 00:14:10.990
Next up, the third match is...

00:14:10.990 --> 00:14:14.450
Team Gaia Dragon from Miyazono High School,

00:14:14.450 --> 00:14:18.710
versus team Try Fighters from Seiho Academy Middle School.

00:14:20.290 --> 00:14:24.420
Here comes the guy who won the Artistic Gunpla Grand Prix.

00:14:25.300 --> 00:14:26.840
Kousaka Yuuma.

00:14:27.760 --> 00:14:31.350
I thought he quit battling to concentrate on building.

00:14:31.760 --> 00:14:34.260
So you came to see your rival?

00:14:34.770 --> 00:14:35.890
Mr. Sudou!

00:14:36.890 --> 00:14:40.940
I had some errands around here.                          I'm just stopping by.

00:14:41.020 --> 00:14:43.400
If you say so, fine.

00:14:43.400 --> 00:14:45.440
Sekai, go for it!

00:14:45.440 --> 00:14:47.440
I'm here with you!

00:14:47.030 --> 00:14:48.700
<b>Sekai!</b>

00:14:47.030 --> 00:14:48.700
<b>Sekai!</b>

00:14:48.700 --> 00:14:51.200
Sekai. Who's that?

00:14:51.370 --> 00:14:52.780
Aren't they cheering for Yuuma?

00:14:53.830 --> 00:14:54.950
Th-That guy...

00:14:55.580 --> 00:14:57.370
The one I met at G-Muse.

00:14:59.870 --> 00:15:03.250
Yuuma's teaming up with that loser?

00:15:03.250 --> 00:15:04.960
He'll lose for sure.

00:15:07.670 --> 00:15:09.470
The Gunpla Battle Championships.

00:15:10.300 --> 00:15:13.470
Yuu, Sekai, thank you.

00:15:13.470 --> 00:15:16.010
Thanks to you two, I stand here today.

00:15:16.640 --> 00:15:19.810
But this isn't the goal. It's a start.

00:15:19.810 --> 00:15:22.060
I want to aim higher and higher.

00:15:23.310 --> 00:15:25.650
Team Try Fighters, let's win!

00:15:25.900 --> 00:15:26.650
Yeah!

00:15:26.820 --> 00:15:27.780
Mission accepted.

00:15:28.320 --> 00:15:29.820
Team Try Fighters!

00:15:30.240 --> 00:15:31.570
Go fight!

00:15:32.360 --> 00:15:35.370
<i>Gunpla Battle, combat mode, startup.</i>

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:38.120
<i>Model damage level, set to B.</i>

00:15:38.620 --> 00:15:40.460
<i>Please set your GP base.</i>

00:15:42.210 --> 00:15:45.090
<i>Beginning Plavsky particle dispersal.</i>

00:15:45.540 --> 00:15:47.840
Field 1, Space.

00:15:48.630 --> 00:15:50.300
<i>Please set your Gunpla.</i>

00:15:52.760 --> 00:15:53.840
<i>Battle start.</i>

00:15:56.560 --> 00:15:58.680
Hoshino Fumina, Winning Gundam!

00:16:02.020 --> 00:16:04.610
Kousaka Yuuma, Lightning Gundam!

00:16:05.230 --> 00:16:08.230
Kamiki Sekai, Build Burning Gundam!

00:16:09.070 --> 00:16:10.570
Team Try Fighters.

00:16:10.570 --> 00:16:12.240
Let's go!

00:16:17.200 --> 00:16:19.790
That's Kousaka Yuuma's Gunpla.

00:16:23.210 --> 00:16:25.130
Is it a custom based on the Zeta?

00:16:25.460 --> 00:16:28.130
No, on the the Re-GZ from Char's Counterattack.

00:16:28.130 --> 00:16:28.880
I see.

00:16:29.500 --> 00:16:31.090
It's certainly built well.

00:16:31.090 --> 00:16:34.930
But I'm more interested in that red Gunpla.

00:16:35.090 --> 00:16:36.300
Red Gunpla?

00:16:37.050 --> 00:16:39.180
What's this perfection?

00:16:39.350 --> 00:16:41.350
Its quality is world-level.

00:16:41.640 --> 00:16:43.730
Did Yuuma build that, too?

00:16:44.060 --> 00:16:47.650
No, I've seen that machine somewhere before...

00:16:48.020 --> 00:16:50.070
Miss Fumina changed her machine.

00:16:50.400 --> 00:16:51.690
It's a support unit.

00:16:51.690 --> 00:16:53.200
It's a booster.

00:16:53.200 --> 00:16:56.450
You boldly changed your machine, Fumina.

00:16:56.700 --> 00:16:59.450
You've become a team of unique individuals.

00:16:59.790 --> 00:17:03.410
Now then, what kind of battle are you going to show us...

00:17:03.750 --> 00:17:05.370
Try Fighters?

00:17:08.670 --> 00:17:10.380
Our first opponent is Miyazono High.

00:17:10.380 --> 00:17:12.380
Their team has a great balance.

00:17:12.670 --> 00:17:14.380
So we should be careful, huh?

00:17:16.300 --> 00:17:18.930
Spread out! Yuu, support from the rear.

00:17:18.930 --> 00:17:19.930
I'll go ahead!

00:17:19.930 --> 00:17:20.350
What?

00:17:20.680 --> 00:17:23.930
In space, Sekai's kenpo is no use.

00:17:24.310 --> 00:17:26.140
But my machine...

00:17:26.650 --> 00:17:28.690
isn't just for long-range shooting!

00:17:33.610 --> 00:17:34.740
It became an airplane!

00:17:34.740 --> 00:17:36.240
That's Yuu's Gunpla!?

00:17:48.630 --> 00:17:50.290
Its performance is as great as rumored.

00:17:50.290 --> 00:17:53.630
Having one great machine doesn't win a battle.

00:17:56.760 --> 00:17:58.640
First, shoot the small one!

00:17:59.010 --> 00:17:59.850
Hoshino!

00:17:59.850 --> 00:18:00.680
Don't worry.

00:18:01.390 --> 00:18:04.390
You've show me how you feel, Yuu.

00:18:05.020 --> 00:18:09.310
Now it's my turn to show my feelings!

00:18:09.560 --> 00:18:12.480
And the power of Winning, which will bring us victory!

00:18:20.620 --> 00:18:23.540
What!? It turned into an SD Gundam!?

00:18:23.830 --> 00:18:25.870
This is my own Gunpla...

00:18:26.250 --> 00:18:27.870
the one I invented!

00:18:34.630 --> 00:18:37.420
She built all of that without anyone's help?

00:18:37.880 --> 00:18:39.220
Well done, Fumi.

00:18:39.510 --> 00:18:41.010
But meanwhile...

00:18:50.060 --> 00:18:50.980
Move away, Sekai!

00:18:51.520 --> 00:18:52.650
I'll shoot it down!

00:18:52.650 --> 00:18:53.520
No way.

00:18:53.520 --> 00:18:54.270
What!?

00:18:54.820 --> 00:18:55.940
I can do it.

00:18:56.490 --> 00:18:58.610
You'll see the results of my training!

00:18:59.360 --> 00:19:01.030
I thought about...

00:19:01.570 --> 00:19:04.280
what I can do, and what Build Burning can do.

00:19:04.870 --> 00:19:06.080
And I figured it out...!

00:19:21.550 --> 00:19:23.140
What's that move?!

00:19:23.470 --> 00:19:24.640
That move!

00:19:25.220 --> 00:19:26.220
It is...

00:19:27.270 --> 00:19:29.730
It's running through space!

00:19:29.890 --> 00:19:32.270
The Gunpla's and the fighter's movements...

00:19:32.560 --> 00:19:34.940
They're in perfect sync.

00:19:34.940 --> 00:19:35.940
Impossible...

00:19:38.530 --> 00:19:40.110
Jigen Haoh style!

00:19:40.320 --> 00:19:43.120
<i>Ryusei Rasen-Ken: Meteor Spiral Fist</i>

00:19:40.320 --> 00:19:43.120
Ryusei Rasen-Ken!

00:19:47.830 --> 00:19:49.660
I thought you were a loser!

00:20:01.590 --> 00:20:03.590
All that particle emission.

00:20:04.300 --> 00:20:06.720
There's no doubt it's based on...

00:20:07.310 --> 00:20:12.440
The machine Iori Sei used in the 11th World Tournament!

00:20:27.030 --> 00:20:28.290
<i>Battle ended.</i>

00:20:30.790 --> 00:20:35.330
The winner is team Try Fighters of Seiho Academy Middle School.

00:20:36.420 --> 00:20:38.300
Wow! You're so cool, Sekai!

00:20:38.500 --> 00:20:42.630
You showed me your Gunpla spirit.

00:20:43.880 --> 00:20:46.430
Sekai, how did you do that move?

00:20:46.430 --> 00:20:48.930
Like I said, it's my special training.

00:20:49.930 --> 00:20:52.350
It seems you're no ordinary idiot.

00:20:52.350 --> 00:20:53.940
Admit that it was great!

00:20:53.940 --> 00:20:55.060
Shut up, amateur.

00:20:55.060 --> 00:20:56.310
What did you say!?

00:21:02.860 --> 00:21:05.490
Yuu, Sekai, thank you!

00:21:05.490 --> 00:21:07.950
Thanks to you two being here, we won.

00:21:07.950 --> 00:21:10.200
This is the first time I've ever made it past round one!

00:21:13.040 --> 00:21:14.660
Let's keep winning, Hoshino.

00:21:15.500 --> 00:21:17.710
I'll keep my promise.

00:21:17.960 --> 00:21:18.840
Okay...

00:21:19.540 --> 00:21:20.500
Thank you.

00:21:27.340 --> 00:21:31.010
Yuuma Kousaka isn't our only foe.

00:21:32.390 --> 00:21:34.390
Even so, we'll win.

00:21:36.730 --> 00:21:38.860
Team Try Fighters, huh?

00:21:40.020 --> 00:21:44.190
I came because I heard the Blue Giant was coaching them.

00:21:44.570 --> 00:21:47.280
They're quite an interesting team.

00:21:48.490 --> 00:21:51.490
Don't you think so, Lady?

00:23:33.600 --> 00:23:34.970
Long time no see.

00:23:38.770 --> 00:23:41.640
Sakai Minato. Why...?

00:23:42.440 --> 00:23:44.360
It doesn't matter why.

00:23:44.650 --> 00:23:47.320
Why are you in the championship?

00:23:48.440 --> 00:23:50.700
Are you trying to flee from competing with me?

00:23:50.950 --> 00:23:53.570
Hey, answer me, Yuuma!

00:24:00.410 --> 00:24:02.830
Our next opponent has won a tournament in the past.

00:24:02.830 --> 00:24:04.880
The team is called...

00:24:04.880 --> 00:24:06.880
Next Episode, "Ruler of the Battlefield."

00:24:06.880 --> 00:24:08.130
Whatever trick awaits us,

00:24:08.130 --> 00:24:09.510
we won't lose!
